 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Try starting with simple shapes first, like lines and circles, and move on to more detailed images as you feel confident. Start at the middle line and build up, or start on a clean page after the main lines are done. Whichever you choose, start from the same spot so it feels coherent. Think of it as depth rather than height. Imagine looking down a deep well instead of straight at you. Simple lines leading away from the eyes help sell the depth. Enjoy the practice, and don't beat yourself up if you don't sell it at first. Drawing is all about repetition.",
